/C [ 0 0 0 ] /Contents (Our question is simple to state: can a system learn a correction without breaking things it already does?\012The longer-term ambition is an agent that can also decide when to intervene, when to hold back, and what\012to investigate next. That brings together the three subjects of the conference session: active inference,\012predictive coding, and heavy-tailed distributions.\012\012Today I want to show you enough of the machinery and the actual outputs to judge the story for yourselves.\012This is the longer colleague version of a talk I will give in Binghamton on October 15. As we go, please\012remember one example or result you would keep in a fifteen-minute version, and one place where the\012explanation loses you. I will pause twice for quick reactions and leave the broader discussion until the end.) /Name Comment /QuadPoints [ 1218 675 1235 675 1218 692 1235 692 ] /Rect [ 1218 675 1235 692 ] /Subtype /Text 
  /Type /Annot
>>
endobj
