/C [ 0 0 0 ] /Contents (Here is the route through the talk. Active inference asks what an agent should do next, given what it\012believes, what it wants, and what it might learn. Predictive coding asks how prediction errors can guide\012updates within a system. Heavy-tail analysis asks about the distribution of consequences, especially\012uncommon large ones that a mean can hide.\012\012Our evidence is at different stages for those three questions. We have a working correction testbed.\012We have experiments that change the learning rule and measure the resulting trade-offs. We also have\012saved probability distributions that let us examine rare harmful changes. The autonomous action-selection\012loop remains a proposal. Making that distinction helps us say what we have learned without treating the\012motivation as a completed result. I will first make the testbed concrete, then show the extremes, then\012the predictive-coding results, and finally reconnect them to the proposed agent.) /Name Comment /QuadPoints [ 1218 675 1235 675 1218 692 1235 692 ] /Rect [ 1218 675 1235 692 ] /Subtype /Text 
  /Type /Annot
>>
endobj
