/C [ 0 0 0 ] /Contents (The central comparison puts a learned reader beside a random-geometry reader with a gate and an older\012stable cap. The main-condition transformer is frozen GPT-2 small. There are additional controls, but\012these three make the main question easiest to see: how much useful retrieval comes from learning the\012reader rather than just having writable memory?\012\012We use three datasets with different prompting styles. The zsRE task uses questions. CounterFact uses\012counterfactual sentence completions and paraphrases. MQuAKE contributes single-hop edits from its data;\012our experiment is not a test of its full multi-hop reasoning task. The first two reach a thousand edits;\012MQuAKE is reported descriptively at three hundred.\012\012Three separately drawn subject realizations are each run in five orders. Those orders can reveal order\012sensitivity, but they reuse facts. Later reader-training seeds also reuse one exposed subject realization.\012Those are useful controlled interventions, with a narrower generalization claim. I will mark the different\012populations rather than combine all the runs as though they were one larger independent experiment.) /Name Comment /QuadPoints [ 1218 675 1235 675 1218 692 1235 692 ] /Rect [ 1218 675 1235 692 ] /Subtype /Text 
  /Type /Annot
>>
endobj
