22 0 obj
<<
/C [ 0 0 0 ] /Contents (Each small point is a subject realization after averaging its five orders. The large marks show the\012mean of the three realizations. Keeping those points visible is more informative here than showing a\012large sample size built from repeated questions or tokens.\012\012The learned-reader result is strongest on zsRE, with about ninety-six percent paraphrase retention.\012CounterFact is about sixty-eight percent. MQuAKE is about seventy-two percent, at its separate\012three-hundred-edit endpoint. These numbers are scores on the supplied targets, not a general knowledge\012or reasoning benchmark. The graph also shows how much the comparisons depend on the dataset.\012\012The useful result is that the learned reader can carry many corrections beyond the exact teaching\012wording. The next question is what changed elsewhere in the model's predictions. The main study's\012limited-realization inference is preliminary; this graph deliberately shows descriptive realization\012spread, not a new confidence interval. A later fourth-realization check against the random reader is\012available in the backup slides, without rewriting the original analysis.) /Name Comment /QuadPoints [ 1218 675 1235 675 1218 692 1235 692 ] /Rect [ 1218 675 1235 692 ] /Subtype /Text 
  /Type /Annot
>>
endobj
