27 0 obj
<<
/C [ 0 0 0 ] /Contents (The left panel shows the fraction of positions where loss rises by more than one hundredth of a nat.\012The right panel asks how large the increase is among those positions. For the learned reader, the\012frequencies are about zero point sixteen percent on zsRE and zero point thirty percent on CounterFact.\012The corresponding conditional severities are about one point six and one point nine nats.\012\012The random reader on CounterFact is worse on both displayed measures. The stable cap on CounterFact has\012no observed harm in this inventory, but it also has zero paraphrase retention. Quietness alone is therefore\012not our goal. On zsRE, different summaries give a less uniform ranking: the learned reader can improve\012editing while increasing some harm summaries relative to stable memory.\012\012Every cell reuses the same ordinary-text inventory. The positions are dependent, and reusing them does\012not multiply the number of independent subjects. These plotted values describe this fixed inventory.\012The full report retains signed improvements, zeros, maxima and expected shortfalls as well as the two\012quantities shown here.) /Name Comment /QuadPoints [ 1218 675 1235 675 1218 692 1235 692 ] /Rect [ 1218 675 1235 692 ] /Subtype /Text 
  /Type /Annot
>>
endobj
