35 0 obj
<<
/C [ 0 0 0 ] /Contents (We selected the mixture using development data and then evaluated it on ten exposed memories: two\012datasets and five orders, at three hundred edits. The graph shows mean severity among positions with\012loss increase above one hundredth of a nat. On zsRE it falls from about one point six two to zero point\012five four nats. On CounterFact it falls from about one point nine three to zero point five eight.\012That is roughly one-third of the original severity, not a reduction of only one-third.\012\012All ten memories meet the specified retention and preservation rule. The frequency of harmful changes\012barely moves. CounterFact paraphrase retention has a small cost, and its mean KL still exceeds the\012benchmark. We also tried a kappa-based bounded-surprisal training loss. That pilot missed its declared\012success rule. It was not the complete coupled-entropy or coupled-free-energy objective proposed in the\012theoretical programme.\012\012The distinction matters: one result is a useful analytic bound with a measured trade-off; the other is\012a negative pilot on a particular loss. Neither is a general verdict on coupled active inference.) /Name Comment /QuadPoints [ 1218 675 1235 675 1218 692 1235 692 ] /Rect [ 1218 675 1235 692 ] /Subtype /Text 
  /Type /Annot
>>
endobj
