39 0 obj
<<
/C [ 0 0 0 ] /Contents (An earlier error in the PC implementation penalized the inferred error plus the existing write, rather\012than penalizing the inferred error alone. That changes the objective when a write is already present.\012We corrected it before the supplemental comparisons shown here. The main feedforward reader experiment\012did not use this defective credit path.\012\012There is a simple mechanism check. At zero inferred error, the quadratic penalty has zero derivative.\012The first gradient step is therefore minus the step size times the adjoint. Our common normalization\012removes that positive scale, so the first-step directions agree in exact arithmetic. In the actual\012one-step runs, all recorded behavioral endpoints agree, while small floating-point differences remain\012in some harm vectors. This makes one step an informative baseline. Any benefit from deeper settling\012must earn its extra cost; it cannot be assumed from the presence of an iterative algorithm.) /Name Comment /QuadPoints [ 1218 675 1235 675 1218 692 1235 692 ] /Rect [ 1218 675 1235 692 ] /Subtype /Text 
  /Type /Annot
>>
endobj
