42 0 obj
<<
/C [ 0 0 0 ] /Contents (These are the same zsRE subjects and the same order at depths one, eight and thirty-two, averaged over\012three realizations. On the left, own-prompt retention rises with deeper settling. Paraphrase retention\012does not show the same gain and falls at thirty-two steps. The other panels show the cost: expected\012shortfall of positive harm rises, and learning takes much longer.\012\012Expected shortfall here means the average of the worst one percent of positive-part loss values across\012the whole inventory, including zeros. It is not the ninety-ninth percentile and not a mean over only the\012positive observations. This older base uses a smaller ordinary-text inventory, so do not compare its\012absolute tail values with the main GPT-2 study as if only the learning rule changed.\012\012The main eight-step comparison across all five orders found about a two-percentage-point own-prompt\012gain on zsRE, with no consistent paraphrase gain. Random-direction credit mostly failed in its one\012attempted stream. The extra-update adjoint control was offered the PC budget but stopped early, so it\012does not settle the question of credit direction versus equal realized compute. Those details are in backup.) /Name Comment /QuadPoints [ 1218 675 1235 675 1218 692 1235 692 ] /Rect [ 1218 675 1235 692 ] /Subtype /Text 
  /Type /Annot
>>
endobj
