47 0 obj
<<
/C [ 0 0 0 ] /Contents (This experiment changes a different part of the system. We trained the reader and controller with\012backpropagation or with error inference, using paired initializations and the same training episodes.\012Acquisition used adjoint credit in both conditions. The left panel shows the difference in paraphrase\012retention for each training seed, with error inference minus backpropagation as the sign convention.\012\012On CounterFact, every seed is lower with the PC-trained reader: by about twenty-four, two and seventeen\012and a half percentage points. zsRE has two small deficits and one small gain. The right panel shows the\012measured training-time ratio: roughly one hundred times as much process time for error inference.\012Each PC training took about a day, compared with roughly fifteen minutes for BP.\012\012The harm results do not provide a uniform compensation: CounterFact harm directions change across seeds.\012Some zsRE PC readers are very quiet, but quietness can accompany missed useful corrections. Three paired\012training seeds help reveal that variability; they are not three independent subject populations. This is\012a substantive negative result for this implementation and recipe. It does not rule out other PC\012architectures, tuning choices, or learning formulations.) /Name Comment /QuadPoints [ 1218 675 1235 675 1218 692 1235 692 ] /Rect [ 1218 675 1235 692 ] /Subtype /Text 
  /Type /Annot
>>
endobj
