/C [ 0 0 0 ] /Contents (We also tested the idea that the cap might benefit from using only higher transformer layers. The design\012crosses two choices: read all three taps or only the upper two, and write at all three sites or only the\012last one. There are three paired seeds and two datasets, for twenty-four evaluations, including shared\012BP controls.\012\012The graph isolates the write comparison. Every pair has more mean ordinary-text loss with last-site-only\012writes, by about two point six to four point four times. Paraphrase scores barely change in those pairs.\012Reading only upper taps also lowers CounterFact paraphrase retention in all three seeds when writes use\012all sites. This does not support the assumption that the lower interfaces are mostly noise.\012\012There is a scope limit: these readers were trained with a full-write objective. Last-only writes were\012evaluated with newly acquired memories under that restriction, not with a separately optimized last-only\012training objective. A differently trained architecture remains a future question.) /Name Comment /QuadPoints [ 1218 675 1235 675 1218 692 1235 692 ] /Rect [ 1218 675 1235 692 ] /Subtype /Text 
  /Type /Annot
>>
endobj
