56 0 obj
<<
/C [ 0 0 0 ] /Contents (Here are the three points I currently want a conference audience to remember. First, the frozen-prior\012architecture supplies concrete components for an active-inference programme, while autonomous policy\012choice is still a missing piece. Second, predictive coding was tested as an actual intervention in the\012learning machinery. We found trade-offs and substantial costs, rather than a general advantage for the\012tested recipe. Third, rare harmful changes make distributional analysis essential: frequency, severity\012and maxima can tell different stories. A simple probability mixture provides a useful bounded baseline.\012\012The successful corrections are real, the negative results are useful, and the limits shape the next\012experiment. That combination seems more informative than treating either the architecture or the\012theoretical framework as already validated. I would like your help deciding which examples make that\012message most memorable and which technical details are necessary to trust it.) /Name Comment /QuadPoints [ 1218 675 1235 675 1218 692 1235 692 ] /Rect [ 1218 675 1235 692 ] /Subtype /Text 
  /Type /Annot
>>
endobj
