/C [ 0 0 0 ] /Contents (Before we open the discussion, take about forty-five seconds to write down three slide numbers. Which\012one would you keep if I had time for only one detailed example? Which needs a clearer explanation?\012And which would you move to the question period? It is also useful to tell me what claim sounded\012stronger than the evidence actually shown.\012\012I am especially interested in whether the concrete answer examples, the predictive-coding mechanism,\012or the distributional harm story gives you the strongest way into this project. I am not asking you to\012pick the most positive result. A negative result that teaches something important may be the right\012center of the talk. The short conference version must still connect all three themes, but the depth\012can follow what you find worth discussing.\012\012After the writing pause, invite two brief reactions, then open the wider discussion. The remaining\012slides are optional backup on MQuAKE, scoring, PC controls, the fourth-realization check and sources.) /Name Comment /QuadPoints [ 1218 675 1235 675 1218 692 1235 692 ] /Rect [ 1218 675 1235 692 ] /Subtype /Text 
  /Type /Annot
>>
endobj
